  dir_exeicon_err_linux.pcpp - break step of dir_exeicon.pcpp: @exeicon for a
  target that is not Windows (an icon is a Windows resource: a warning, not
  used, the file is not looked for)

  How to check, from repo\bin (the Linux target only: on Windows it applies):
    pcpp res\tests\dir_exeicon_err_linux.pcpp -t x86_64-linux-gnu
  The marked line reports that code; nothing else is reported.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe dir_exeicon_err_linux;
@exeicon "$P:res/assets/icons/paskalcpp.ico"; // WARN SM0103@1: a target that is not Windows

begin
end.
